{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And your brother shall live with you</b> — and adjacent to it: <b>Do not take from him interest or increase</b> — a hint that whoever lends at interest does not live, as it is written: \"He gave at interest, took increase — shall he live? He shall not live.\"" "<b>Interest</b> in gematria is <b>this</b> נחש. In the future the serpent will not be healed, as written: \"and dust the serpent's food\" — so too one who takes interest shall not live. Another interpretation: interest is like the serpent, for it bites like a serpent. רבית (interest) = תרי\"ב, for it is weighed against תרי\"ב commandments."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:36.042196562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}